@event duel_hall_reading_the_floor
# en: Reading the Floor
title [59a276] = 读地板
# en: {Every famous bout in the Duelling Hall left its mark on the floor, a scorch or a frost-crack or a gouge. Old duellists say you can read a fight in the boards.|The floor again. You've learned which scorch belongs to which year's champion, from the plaques on the wall.|You can read the boards now, more or less: here someone parried late; here someone lost their nerve and their eyebrows.} {Today a fresh burn sits on top of the old ones.|The cleaners have been, and the boards shine like a map under glass.|{season == "winter": The hall is freezing and the boards creak under every step.|Dust hangs in the long light from the windows.}}
text [c6e5a9] = {决斗厅里每一场著名对决都在地板上留下了印记，一道焦痕、一道霜裂或一道刻痕。老决斗手说，从地板上就能读出一场对决。|又是这片地板。你已从墙上的铭牌认出哪道焦痕属于哪一年的冠军。|如今你大致读得懂这些木板了：这里有人招架晚了；这里有人丢了胆量，也丢了眉毛。} {今天一道新焦痕压在旧痕上面。|清洁工来过了，木板亮得像压在玻璃下的地图。|{season == "winter": 大厅冷得刺骨，每踩一步木板都吱嘎作响。|窗外斜照进来的长光里浮着灰尘。}}
# en: Scorched and scarred floorboards in an empty duelling hall, a student crouched over them tracing a burn mark with one finger.
scene [a65405] = 空荡荡的决斗厅里，地板满是焦痕与伤痕，一个学生蹲在上面，用一根手指描着一道烧痕。
# en: Trace an old bout through
opt.left.label [a50397] = 把一场旧对决描完
# en: {You follow a duel from the first scorch to the final frost-crack, step by step, until you know where the loser went wrong. Your knees ache from crawling.|You walk a champion's footwork across the burns, slowly, like learning a dance from its footprints. It's tiring, careful work.|You read a whole tournament final in the floor and find the moment it turned, a single mark the size of a coin. You stand up stiff and certain.}
opt.left.say.1 [bb7a9f] = {你从第一道焦痕一路追到最后一道霜裂，一步一步，直到看出输家错在哪里。爬得你膝盖生疼。|你踩着焦痕慢慢走一位冠军的步法，像照着脚印学一支舞。累人又费心的活儿。|你从地板上读完了一整场锦标赛决赛，找到了局势翻转的那一刻：一道硬币大小的痕迹。你站起来时浑身僵硬，心里笃定。}
# en: Scrub the floor for the club
opt.right.label [656163] = 替社团擦地板
# en: {The club pays a crown or two for scrubbing. You scrub until the boards gleam and your arms burn.|You scrub, and the old marks stay, as they always do; the dirt goes. You're paid in coins and a sore back.|You know which boards to go easy on: the famous ones. The club treasurer pays you, and adds a nod.}
opt.right.say.1 [403a2d] = {社团擦地板给一两个克朗。你擦到木板锃亮，胳膊火辣辣的。|你擦啊擦，旧痕照旧留着，一向如此；污垢却没了。你换来几枚硬币和一副酸背。|你知道哪些木板要下手轻些：那些著名的。社团司库付了钱，外加一个点头。}

@event duel_hall_second_wanted
# en: A Second Wanted
title [47af57] = 招一名副手
# en: {{here} has a formal practice bout today and no second. "Hold my coat, count the paces, drop the handkerchief. You can count, I assume."|{here} is looking for a second again, and spots you at the door before you can leave.|{here} tosses you the coat as you come in, as if it's been decided.} {The opponent is an upper-year with a terrible moustache.|The opponent bows too low, which is a kind of insult.|{season == "winter": The hall is so cold the wands spark on their own.|The gallery has a dozen spectators and a bookmaker.}}
text [e5775f] = {{here}今天有一场正式的练习对决，却没有副手。“替我拿外套，数步子，丢手帕。你会数数吧，我想。”|{here}又在找副手了，你还没来得及溜，就在门口被看见了。|你一进门，{here}就把外套扔给你，好像早就说定了。} {对手是个留着可怕小胡子的高年级生。|对手鞠躬鞠得太低，这本身就是一种侮辱。|{season == "winter": 大厅冷得魔杖自己都在冒火星。|看台上有十几个观众和一个庄家。}}
# en: Two students facing each other on a scorched duelling floor, wands lowered, while a third stands at the edge holding a coat and a handkerchief.
scene [f12d32] = 两个学生在焦痕斑斑的决斗场上相对而立，魔杖垂着，第三个人站在场边，拿着一件外套和一块手帕。
# en: Stand as the second
opt.left.label [1211ae] = 当这个副手
# en: {You count, she wins, she doesn't thank you. On the way out she hands you back your scarf, which you hadn't noticed she'd picked up.|She loses on a technicality and blames the handkerchief. Then she buys you a cider, without a word.|You count; she wins in nine seconds. "Adequate," she says, which from Lyra is a medal.}
opt.left.say.1 [f09634] = {你数步子，她赢了，她没道谢。出门时她把你的围巾递还给你，你都没发现她什么时候捡起来的。|她因为一个技术细节输了，怪到手帕头上。然后一言不发地请你喝了杯苹果酒。|你数步子；她九秒就赢了。“还行。”她说。从莱拉嘴里出来，这就是勋章。}
# en: {Bram makes you recite the rules of seconding before he lets you hold his coat. He wins, and gives you a demerit for dropping the handkerchief early, then rescinds it.|Bram loses and stands very straight. Afterwards, gruffly, "Fair count. Thanks."|Bram wins, and for a moment looks up at the gallery as if for someone who isn't there.}
opt.left.say.2 [0530ab] = {布拉姆让你背完副手守则才肯让你拿外套。他赢了，因为你丢手帕早了记你一次过，随即又撤销了。|布拉姆输了，站得笔直。事后他粗声粗气地说：“数得公道。谢了。”|布拉姆赢了，有一瞬间他抬头望向看台，像在找一个不在那里的人。}
# en: {You count the paces, drop the handkerchief and hold the coat through an hour of shouting. {here} owes you one, and knows it.|You stand on the line through a long, sweaty bout. {here} thanks you warmly afterwards.|You second with the calm of long practice. {here} wins, and claps you on the shoulder like an old comrade.}
opt.left.say.3 [dbd567] = {你数步子、丢手帕，在一小时的吼叫声里一直拿着外套。{here}欠你一个人情，TA 自己也知道。|你在线上站完一场漫长又汗流浃背的对决。事后{here}热情地谢了你。|你以多年练就的镇定当好副手。{here}赢了，像拍老战友一样拍拍你的肩。}
# en: Offer to referee instead
opt.right.label [c1d9e4] = 改当裁判
# en: {You referee straight down the middle and call a foul against {here}. The gallery approves. {here} does not.|You referee, fairly, and learn more watching both wands than you would holding a coat. {here} feels a little abandoned.|Your call decides the bout. It's the right call; {here} won't admit it till next week.}
opt.right.say.1 [11abee] = {你不偏不倚地执裁，判了{here}一次犯规。看台赞成。{here}不赞成。|你公正地执裁，同时盯着两根魔杖，学到的比拿外套多得多。{here}觉得有点被抛弃了。|你的判决决定了胜负。判得没错；{here}要到下周才肯承认。}

@event greenhouses_gerald_is_out
# en: Gerald Is Out
title [dff50c] = 杰拉尔德跑出来了
# en: {Gerald, Tobias's mandrake, has escaped his pot again and planted himself among the seedlings. His knitted hat has come unravelled.|Gerald is out again. This time he's in a teacup, screaming softly at a watering can.|Gerald has moved into the pot of the tallest fern, with an air of permanence. His hat is half unravelled; the wool trails back to his own pot.} {Tobias is nowhere to be seen.|A note on Gerald's empty pot says "BACK SOON, DO NOT LET HIM NEAR THE TOMATOES."|{season == "winter": He's shivering, defiantly.|The seedlings around him are wilting with alarm.}}
text [25fad7] = {托比亚斯的曼德拉草杰拉尔德又从盆里逃出来，把自己栽在了幼苗中间。他的针织帽脱线了。|杰拉尔德又跑出来了。这回他待在一只茶杯里，冲着洒水壶轻声尖叫。|杰拉尔德搬进了最高那株蕨的花盆，一副要长住的架势。他的帽子拆了一半，毛线一路拖回他自己的盆。} {托比亚斯不见人影。|杰拉尔德的空盆上贴着字条：“马上回来，别让他靠近番茄。”|{season == "winter": 他冻得发抖，却很倔强。|他周围的幼苗都吓蔫了。}}
# en: A small mandrake in a lopsided knitted hat sitting in the wrong flowerpot among the seedlings, screaming very softly at a watering can.
scene [0de02b] = 一株戴着歪斜针织帽的小曼德拉草坐在幼苗中间一个不属于他的花盆里，对着洒水壶极轻地尖叫。
# en: Fix his hat and carry him home
opt.left.label [9e26ec] = 补好帽子送他回家
# en: {You re-knit the hat with two pencils and great patience. Gerald lets you, then bites your thumb, which Tobias says means he loves you.|You lift him gently out of the teacup. He screams softly the whole way home and bites you once at the end, fondly.|You tie off the trailing wool and carry him home in your cupped hands. The bite is affectionate. It still stings.}
opt.left.say.1 [98879d] = {你用两支铅笔耐心地把帽子重新织好。杰拉尔德任你摆弄，然后咬了你的拇指，托比亚斯说这表示他爱你。|你轻轻把他从茶杯里捧出来。他一路轻声尖叫，到家时深情地咬了你一口。|你把拖着的毛线收好结，把他捧在手心送回家。这一口是出于喜爱。还是很疼。}
# en: Re-pot the seedlings he trampled
opt.right.label [977063] = 把踩坏的幼苗重新栽好
# en: {You leave Gerald where he is and save the seedlings he kicked out. He watches you work, screaming softly with approval.|You re-pot a row of uprooted seedlings and leave the teacup alone. Mandrakes are Tobias's department.|You patch up the damage around the fern and let Gerald keep his new home. It seems kinder than arguing with a mandrake.}
opt.right.say.1 [cc084d] = {你让杰拉尔德待在原处，去救他踢出来的幼苗。他看着你干活，赞许地轻声尖叫。|你重新栽好一排被拔起的幼苗，没去碰那只茶杯。曼德拉草归托比亚斯管。|你修补好那株蕨周围的狼藉，让杰拉尔德留在新家。这似乎比跟一株曼德拉草争论更仁慈。}

@event greenhouses_grafting_bench
# en: The Grafting Bench
title [592530] = 嫁接台
# en: {On the grafting bench is the club's oldest experiment, a potted tree that bears pears on one branch and lemons on the other. Beside it, knives, twine, wax and an open invitation.|The grafting bench. Somebody's new graft has taken: a rose that grows on a gooseberry, looking pleased with itself.|The grafting bench. The two-fruit tree has a third branch now, and nobody will admit to it.} {The wax pot is warm and smells of honey.|A row of failed grafts stands along the back, each with a small apologetic label.|{season == "spring": Every graft on the bench is in bud.|The saplings are bare, and the twine shows.}}
text [dd5537] = {嫁接台上摆着社团最老的实验：一棵盆栽树，一根枝上结梨，另一根结柠檬。旁边放着刀、麻绳、蜡，以及一份公开的邀请。|嫁接台。有人的新嫁接成活了：一朵长在醋栗上的玫瑰，看上去很得意。|嫁接台。那棵双果树长出了第三根枝，谁也不承认是自己干的。} {蜡锅温热，散发着蜂蜜味。|后排站着一溜嫁接失败的作品，每株都挂着一张抱歉的小标签。|{season == "spring": 台上每一处嫁接都冒了芽。|树苗光秃秃的，麻绳露在外面。}}
# en: A potting bench crowded with small grafted saplings bound in twine and wax, one of them bearing two different kinds of fruit on two different branches.
scene [b287e3] = 盆栽台上挤满了用麻绳和蜡绑着的小嫁接树苗，其中一株在两根不同的枝上结着两种不同的果子。
# en: Try a graft of your own
opt.left.label [be2ab7] = 自己试着嫁接
# en: {You splice a cutting of mint onto a lavender root and wax it shut. A week later it's growing; it smells like a summer evening.|Your graft takes. Someone pins a label to it with your name and a small drawn star.|You graft a cutting onto the two-fruit tree itself. It takes, and the tree now has one branch that is entirely yours.}
opt.left.say.1 [9c92ea] = {你把一根薄荷插条嫁到薰衣草根上，用蜡封好。一周后它活了，闻起来像夏日的傍晚。|你的嫁接成活了。有人给它别上一张标签，写着你的名字，还画了颗小星星。|你把一根插条直接嫁到双果树上。它成活了，如今那棵树有一根枝完全属于你。}
# en: {The knife slips; so does the cutting. It joins the row of failures with its own small label, and you join the infirmary queue with a cut thumb.|Your graft sulks, browns and drops off within the week. Your thumb has a nick that takes longer to heal.|The twine won't hold and the wax burns your fingers. Your cutting goes to the failures' shelf.}
opt.left.say.2 [127425] = {刀一滑，插条也滑了。它带着自己的小标签加入了失败者的行列，你则带着割伤的拇指加入了医务室的队伍。|你的嫁接闹了脾气，发褐，一周内就掉了。你拇指上的口子好得更慢。|麻绳绑不住，蜡还烫了你的手指。你的插条被送上了失败者的架子。}
# en: Label the old grafts
opt.right.label [b51afe] = 给旧嫁接贴标签
# en: {You work out from the bark scars which graft went on when, and write it all down. The two-fruit tree is older than anyone thought.|You label the rose on the gooseberry, which turns out to be harder than growing it.|You map the two-fruit tree branch by branch. The third branch has no record at all. You write "unknown, but welcome".}
opt.right.say.1 [5a89f5] = {你从树皮的疤痕推算出每处嫁接是何时做的，一一记下。那棵双果树比谁想的都老。|你给醋栗上的玫瑰贴好标签，这事比把它种出来还难。|你一根枝一根枝地绘出双果树的图谱。第三根枝毫无记录。你写下：“来历不明，但欢迎。”}

@event greenhouses_seed_tin
# en: The Seed Tin
title [8ae9de] = 种子罐
# en: {On the potting bench is the club's seed tin. Take a packet, leave a packet, write what it is; most people write what it is.|The seed tin is fuller than last time. Someone has left a packet labelled simply "SORRY".|The seed tin. You know the regulars' handwriting now, and the one who only draws pictures.} {One packet is rattling on its own.|One packet is warm to the touch.|{season == "spring": Half the packets have started sprouting through the paper.|One packet hums a single note when you lift it.}}
text [36c1b4] = {盆栽台上放着社团的种子罐。拿一包，留一包，写上是什么；大多数人会写。|种子罐比上回满了。有人留了一包，标签只写着“对不起”。|种子罐。你如今认得常客们的笔迹，还有那个只画图的人。} {有一包自己在沙沙响。|有一包摸上去是温的。|{season == "spring": 一半的种子包已经顶破纸发了芽。|有一包你一拿起来就哼出一个音。}}
# en: An old biscuit tin of paper seed packets on a potting bench, every packet labelled in a different hand, one of them rattling on its own.
scene [18baa0] = 盆栽台上一只旧饼干罐里装着纸种子包，每包标签笔迹各异，其中一包自己在沙沙作响。
# en: Take the strangest packet
opt.left.label [0117ca] = 拿最古怪的一包
# en: {You plant it in a spare pot. By the end of the hour there's a tiny silver bell-flower that rings when you breathe on it.|You plant the warm one. It comes up in minutes, a fern that curls round your finger like a cat's tail.|You plant it and it grows into something nobody in the club can name. You get to name it. You choose well.}
opt.left.say.1 [095f50] = {你把它种进一只空盆。一小时后长出一朵小小的银铃花，你朝它呵气它就响。|你种下温热的那包。几分钟就冒了出来，一株蕨像猫尾巴一样卷住你的手指。|你种下它，长出了一样社团里谁也叫不出名的东西。命名权归你。你起了个好名字。}
# en: {It sprouts at once, straight up your nose. You sneeze pollen for the rest of the day.|It grows a single angry thorn and nothing else, and the thorn finds your thumb.|It's a nettle that stings in rhymes. You'll be hearing them in your sleep.}
opt.left.say.2 [1d3743] = {它立刻发芽，直往你鼻子里钻。你一整天都在打喷嚏喷花粉。|它只长出一根气呼呼的刺，别的什么也没有，那根刺找上了你的拇指。|是一株会押韵的荨麻，蜇人时还押韵。你睡梦里都会听见。}
# en: Sort the tin properly
opt.right.label [938cae] = 好好整理罐子
# en: {You sort the packets by family, season and handwriting. The club will never know it was you, which is the nice part.|You sort the lot and label the unlabelled ones. "SORRY" turns out to be turnips, which explains a great deal.|You file the picture-packets by guessing from the drawings. You're right about most of them, you think.}
opt.right.say.1 [b18ef1] = {你按科属、季节和笔迹整理好种子包。社团永远不会知道是你，这正是好处。|你整理完，给没标签的贴上标签。“对不起”原来是萝卜，这就说得通了。|你凭画猜内容，把画图的那些也归了档。你觉得大部分都猜对了。}

@event flight_field_kite_day
# en: Kite Day
title [601850] = 风筝日
# en: {The wind is too wild for brooms, so the first-years are out with charmed kites, paper dragons and fish and one very angry swan.|Kite day again. The kites have learned to fight; a paper dragon has a fish in a headlock.|Whenever the wind is too wild for brooms, the kites come out. You know the swan by now, and the swan knows you.} One kite is stuck in the far hoop, {flapping like a trapped bird|and its first-year is close to tears|and the other kites are jeering at it}.
text [22a775] = {风大得骑不了扫帚，于是一年级生们放起了施了咒的风筝：纸龙、纸鱼，还有一只非常愤怒的天鹅。|又是风筝日。风筝们学会了打架；一条纸龙正用胳膊锁住一条鱼。|每逢风大得骑不了扫帚，风筝就出来了。你认得那只天鹅了，天鹅也认得你。} 有只风筝卡在了远处的圈环上，{像只困住的鸟一样扑腾|它的一年级主人快哭了|其他风筝都在嘲笑它}。
# en: Enchanted paper kites shaped like dragons and fish wheeling and diving over a windswept green field, one tangled in a hoop at the far end.
scene [e11b11] = 被施了咒的龙形、鱼形纸风筝在大风吹拂的绿色场地上空盘旋俯冲，其中一只缠在远端的圈环上。
# en: Climb the hoop and free it
opt.left.label [2bf483] = 爬上圈环救它
# en: {You shin up the hoop pole and free the kite. The first-years cheer as if you'd won a race.|You climb, untangle, slide down. The first-year announces your name to the whole field.|You know the hoop pole's footholds by now. The kite goes back to its owner, who tells everyone, loudly.}
opt.left.say.1 [c7337b] = {你顺着圈环杆爬上去解下风筝。一年级生们欢呼得像你赢了一场比赛。|爬上、解开、滑下。那个一年级生向全场宣布了你的名字。|你如今熟悉圈环杆上的落脚点了。风筝回到主人手里，主人大声告诉了所有人。}
# en: {You get halfway up the pole and the wind takes your hat and your grip. You land in the long grass, bruised.|The kite comes free and so do you, from rather high up.|You slip on the wet pole and slide down it, slowly and painfully, to applause.}
opt.left.say.2 [58ee0e] = {你爬到一半，风卷走了你的帽子和你的抓握。你摔进长草里，青一块紫一块。|风筝解下来了，你也下来了，从相当高的地方。|你在湿杆上一滑，慢慢地、疼痛地一路滑到底，赢得一片掌声。}
# en: Borrow a kite and fly it
opt.right.label [17e46b] = 借只风筝来放
# en: {You borrow a fish kite and steer it with a whispered charm. It bites the swan. Everyone is delighted.|You fly a paper dragon in loops until your arms ache with the pull and your face aches with grinning.|You fly your borrowed kite higher than the rest, holding the charm steady against the gusts.}
opt.right.say.1 [b3c89a] = {你借了一只鱼风筝，低声念咒操纵它。它咬了天鹅一口。大家都乐坏了。|你让一条纸龙翻着筋斗飞，拽得胳膊酸，笑得脸也酸。|你把借来的风筝放得比谁都高，迎着阵风稳住咒语。}

@event flight_field_mowing_day
# en: Mowing Day
title [75faec] = 割草日
# en: {Today the enchanted scythes are mowing the Flight Field, swinging themselves in neat lines while the groundskeeper sleeps under a tree.|Mowing day. A game has sprung up among the scythes: run the line without breaking stride. The groundskeeper is asleep again.|The scythes are out. You know their rhythm now: swish, step, swish, a pause on every seventh.} {The smell of cut grass is everywhere.|Somebody's hat has already been mown in half.|{season == "summer": Heat shimmers over the stubble.|A light drizzle makes the grass shine.}}
text [9c9f9f] = {今天施了咒的镰刀在给飞行场割草，自己排成整齐的行列挥舞，场地管理员在树下睡大觉。|割草日。镰刀之间兴起了一个游戏：不停步地穿过那一排。管理员又睡着了。|镰刀出动了。你如今熟悉它们的节奏：唰、迈步、唰，每到第七下停一拍。} {到处都是青草刚割过的气味。|已经有人的帽子被齐齐割成了两半。|{season == "summer": 热浪在草茬上方晃动。|一阵细雨让草地闪闪发亮。}}
# en: A row of enchanted scythes swinging themselves across a green field in neat lines while students dart between them and others rake the cut grass.
scene [b91665] = 一排施了咒的镰刀自己挥舞着，在绿色场地上割出整齐的行列，学生们在镰刀间穿梭，另一些人在耙割下的草。
# en: Run the scythe line
opt.left.label [bd2127] = 穿过镰刀阵
# en: {You dart through the line and out the other side without a scratch. The watching first-years make you do it again.|Swish, step, swish. You run the whole line and arrive at the end breathless and laughing.|You run the line on the seventh-beat pause and it feels like dancing. Nobody else has timed it that well.}
opt.left.say.1 [0ea5bf] = {你从镰刀阵中一穿而过，毫发无损。围观的一年级生非要你再来一次。|唰、迈步、唰。你跑完整排，到头时上气不接下气，笑个不停。|你踩着第七拍的停顿穿过去，像在跳舞。没人把时机掐得这么准过。}
# en: {A scythe catches your robe and neatly removes a sleeve. You trip on the stump of it. The groundskeeper wakes, looks, and goes back to sleep.|You trip on a tussock and fall flat as the scythes pass politely overhead. The first-years cheer, the wrong way.|You mistime the seventh beat and go sprawling. Your hat joins the other hat. Your pride follows.}
opt.left.say.2 [c8c1be] = {一把镰刀勾住你的袍子，利落地削掉一只袖子。你被那截残袖绊了一跤。管理员醒来看了一眼，又睡了。|你被草墩绊倒，扑倒在地，镰刀们彬彬有礼地从你头顶掠过。一年级生们欢呼了，方向不对。|你错过了第七拍，摔了个四仰八叉。你的帽子和另一顶帽子作了伴。你的自尊也跟了过去。}
# en: Rake hay for the stables
opt.right.label [5c7bd2] = 替马厩耙干草
# en: {You rake the cut grass into rows for the stables. The groundskeeper wakes long enough to give you a coin and a nod. Your palms blister.|You rake until the field is striped and your arms are lead. The stables send a crown, and a hippogriff's thanks.|You rake with the scythes' rhythm in your arms. The groundskeeper pays you without waking, which is a skill in itself.}
opt.right.say.1 [a84100] = {你把割下的草耙成一行行，给马厩用。管理员醒来片刻，给了你一枚硬币和一个点头。你的手掌起了泡。|你耙到整片场地都成了条纹，胳膊沉得像灌了铅。马厩送来一个克朗，外加一头鹰头马身有翼兽的谢意。|你的胳膊里带着镰刀的节奏耙草。管理员没醒就把钱付了，这本身就是一门手艺。}

@event secret_garden_two_cups
# en: Two Cups on the Bench
title [100ec2] = 长凳上的两只杯子
# en: {On the bench by the humming pear there's a flask and two chipped cups, and a note in Old Maud's hand. "One for you, dearie, one for whoever comes."|The flask on the bench again, still warm, still with two cups. Maud is never here when you are; the tea always is.|The flask, the cups, the note, and today a biscuit on a saucer beside them, for whoever comes.} {The silver bees are busy.|The ferns are glowing even in daylight.|{season == "winter": Frost on the bench, steam from the flask.|Blossom has settled in one of the cups.}}
text [65f1d7] = {会哼歌的梨树旁的长凳上放着一只保温壶、两只缺口的杯子，还有老莫德亲笔写的字条。“一杯给你，亲爱的，一杯给后来的人。”|长凳上又是那只保温壶，还温着，还是两只杯子。你来时莫德从不在；茶却总在。|保温壶、杯子、字条，今天旁边的碟子里还多了一块饼干，留给后来的人。} {银蜜蜂忙个不停。|蕨类连白天都在发光。|{season == "winter": 长凳上结着霜，壶口冒着热气。|一只杯子里落了几片花瓣。}}
# en: A mossy stone bench in a hidden garden, an old tartan flask and two chipped cups left on it, glowing ferns all around.
scene [2e0281] = 隐秘花园里一条长满青苔的石凳，上面放着一只旧格子保温壶和两只缺口的杯子，四周是发光的蕨类。
# en: Sit and drink the tea
opt.left.label [043f61] = 坐下喝茶
# en: {The tea tastes of honey and something green. You sit till the cup is cold and feel mended in some small, specific way.|You drink your cup and leave the second for whoever comes. Nobody does, but the pear hums as if someone had.|You drink, eat the biscuit, and wash both cups at the spring. The garden seems to approve of good manners.}
opt.left.say.1 [91c359] = {茶有蜂蜜和某种青草的味道。你坐到杯子凉透，觉得自己在某个细小而具体的地方被修补好了。|你喝了自己那杯，把另一杯留给后来的人。没人来，可梨树哼得像是有人来过。|你喝茶、吃饼干，在泉边把两只杯子都洗了。花园似乎很赞赏好礼数。}
# en: Weed the beds for her
opt.right.label [d74fa1] = 替她除草
# en: {You leave the tea and weed the beds by the wall until your knees are green and your back is stiff. Maud will know, somehow.|You pull weeds that pull back, and one of them draws blood. The ferns lean away from the worst of them, gratefully.|You weed the far beds until your palms blister, and find a trowel Maud must have lost years ago. You leave it on the bench, by the cups.}
opt.right.say.1 [6b4155] = {你没喝茶，去墙边的花床除草，直到膝盖都染绿了，腰也僵了。莫德总会知道的。|你拔的草会反拽回来，有一株还扎出了血。蕨类感激地躲开最凶的那几株。|你给远处的花床除草，直到手掌起泡，找到一把莫德多年前弄丢的小铲子。你把它放在长凳上，杯子旁边。}

@event secret_garden_remembering_moss
# en: The Moss That Remembers
title [d9ae53] = 记得人的苔藓
# en: {Under the humming pear is a bed of moss so thick it keeps the shape of whoever last lay in it. Today it holds a small curled shape, like someone napping.|The moss again. Today's shape is long and straight, arms folded, as if someone lay there watching the leaves.|You know the moss's habits now. Today it holds two shapes, side by side, close.} {The shapes fade slowly, over an hour or so.|One silver bee is asleep in the hollow of an elbow.|{season == "winter": Frost rims the shape like a chalk outline.|The moss is warm where the shape is.}}
text [7cdb7b] = {会哼歌的梨树下有一片苔藓，厚得能留住最后躺在上面的人的形状。今天它留着一个小小的蜷缩的形状，像有人在这儿打过盹。|又是那片苔藓。今天的形状又长又直，双臂交叠，像有人躺在这儿看树叶。|你如今摸清了苔藓的脾性。今天它留着两个形状，并排着，挨得很近。} {这些形状会慢慢褪去，大约一个钟头。|一只银蜜蜂睡在一只手肘的凹陷里。|{season == "winter": 霜沿着形状结了一圈，像粉笔描的轮廓。|有形状的地方，苔藓是温的。}}
# en: A deep green bed of moss under the humming pear tree, holding the faint pressed shape of someone who lay there and is gone.
scene [638731] = 会哼歌的梨树下一片深绿的厚苔藓，上面压着一个淡淡的人形，躺过的人已经离开了。
# en: Lie down in the moss yourself
opt.left.label [0de546] = 自己躺进苔藓里
# en: {You lie down beside the curled shape, not in it. The moss is warm and soft, and you sleep a while without dreaming.|You lie down and look up at the pear tree's leaves for an hour. When you get up, the moss keeps your shape too.|You lie down between the two shapes, careful not to spoil either. You wake rested, and a little lonely.}
opt.left.say.1 [b1d6ed] = {你躺在那个蜷缩的形状旁边，而不是躺进去。苔藓温暖柔软，你无梦地睡了一会儿。|你躺下来望着梨树的叶子看了一个钟头。起身时，苔藓也留下了你的形状。|你躺在两个形状之间，小心不去破坏任何一个。醒来时你歇足了，也有点寂寞。}
# en: Study the shapes, and wonder
opt.right.label [ce8781] = 端详形状，暗自揣想
# en: {You kneel and read the shape. Small hands, knees drawn up, a hat left behind in the dent of a head. Someone came here to feel safe. It's a strange thing to know about a stranger.|You trace the long shape's folded arms. It looks like someone thinking very hard about something they couldn't say. You leave quietly.|Two shapes, close. You don't know whose, and you decide you shouldn't. It stays with you all evening.}
opt.right.say.1 [49088b] = {你跪下来读那个形状：小小的手，蜷起的膝盖，头部的凹陷里落下一顶帽子。有人来这里寻求安全感。知道一个陌生人的这种事，感觉很奇妙。|你描着那个长形状交叠的双臂。它像是某个人在苦苦思索一件说不出口的事。你悄悄离开了。|两个形状，挨得很近。你不知道是谁，也决定自己不该知道。这念头陪了你一整晚。}

@event secret_garden_snail_post
# en: The Snail Post
title [0a39a1] = 蜗牛邮政
# en: {A snail is crossing the garden wall with a folded scrap of paper tucked under its shell. Maud's garden, it seems, has a postal service.|The snail post again. Three snails today, each with a note, all heading in different directions.|Snail post. You know the route now, along the wall and round the pear, about a day each way.} {The note within reach is folded twice and sealed with a blob of resin.|One note has been answered in a different hand.|{season == "winter": The snails are sluggish with cold, the notes damp.|The snail nearest you is wearing a dewdrop like a hat.}}
text [988231] = {一只蜗牛正爬过花园的墙，壳底下塞着一张折好的纸片。看来莫德的花园有自己的邮政。|又是蜗牛邮政。今天有三只蜗牛，各驮一张字条，各奔东西。|蜗牛邮政。你如今熟悉路线了：沿着墙，绕过梨树，单程大约一天。} {你够得着的那张折了两折，用一滴树脂封着。|有一张字条被另一种笔迹回复了。|{season == "winter": 蜗牛冻得慢吞吞的，字条也潮了。|离你最近的那只蜗牛顶着一颗露珠，像戴了顶帽子。}}
# en: A garden snail with a tiny folded paper note tucked under its shell, making its way slowly along a mossy wall.
scene [3444e6] = 一只花园蜗牛壳下塞着一张折好的小字条，正沿着长满青苔的墙慢慢爬行。
# en: Write a note and send it on
opt.left.label [7db9c8] = 写张字条寄出去
# en: {You write something kind for a stranger and tuck it under a shell. The snail sets off, at snail speed, with your secret.|You answer a note left by someone you'll never meet. It feels like talking across a very slow, very gentle river.|You write back to whoever's been writing. The snail takes the note, and an age, and you don't mind.}
opt.left.say.1 [2fdf73] = {你给一个陌生人写了句好话，塞进壳底。蜗牛以蜗牛的速度出发，带着你的秘密。|你回复了一个你永远不会见到的人留下的字条。就像隔着一条非常缓慢、非常温柔的河说话。|你给那个一直在写信的人回了信。蜗牛接过字条，慢得要命，你也不在意。}
# en: Read the notes on the way
opt.right.label [76b094] = 半路偷看字条
# en: {You ease a note out from under a shell. It's a confession about a stolen apple, decades old. You put it back, a little ashamed.|You read three notes before the snails notice. One of them is about someone exactly like you.|You read the snail post like a gossip column. The snails take it personally; one refuses to move till you leave.}
opt.right.say.1 [7fda3d] = {你从壳底轻轻抽出一张字条。是几十年前偷了一个苹果的忏悔。你把它塞回去，有点惭愧。|你在蜗牛察觉前读了三张。其中一张写的人和你一模一样。|你把蜗牛邮政当八卦专栏读。蜗牛们很介意；有一只赌气不动，直到你离开。}

@event courier_loft_record_board
# en: The Record Board
title [5cf4e9] = 纪录板
# en: {On the loft wall is the record board, the fastest delivery ever flown to every tower and the village, in chalk. The village record is eleven minutes. It has stood for twelve years.|The record board. Someone has shaved four seconds off the observatory run and written the new time very large.|The record board. You know every time on it now, and which ones the couriers say were cheated.} {A courier is idly offering a parcel to anyone who fancies a go.|The wind outside is behind you, for once.|{season == "winter": There's ice on the landing platform.|The air is still and the lake is glass.}}
text [dbf5ff] = {阁楼墙上是纪录板，用粉笔写着飞往每座塔和镇上的最快送件时间。镇上的纪录是十一分钟，已经保持了十二年。|纪录板。有人把观星台航线的纪录缩短了四秒，新时间写得很大。|纪录板。如今上面每个时间你都熟悉，也知道信使们说哪些是作弊得来的。} {有个信使懒洋洋地拿着一个包裹，问谁想试试。|外面的风难得是顺风。|{season == "winter": 起降台上结了冰。|空气静止，湖面像玻璃。}}
# en: A chalkboard in a draughty loft listing delivery records to every tower and the village, some times rubbed out and rewritten, a student squinting at the fastest one.
scene [9b9e40] = 漏风的阁楼里一块粉笔板列着飞往每座塔和镇上的送件纪录，有些时间被擦掉重写，一个学生眯眼看着最快的那个。
# en: Make a run at a record
opt.left.label [ba9752] = 冲击一项纪录
# en: {You fly the lecture-tower run flat out and land four seconds inside the record. A courier chalks your name on the board, grumbling.|You take the observatory run, cut the corner by the bell tower and beat the new time by a breath. The loft cheers; the old record holder sulks.|You know the shortcuts now. Your name goes up on the board for the library run, in very large chalk.}
opt.left.say.1 [529c7f] = {你全速飞完讲堂塔航线，落地时比纪录快了四秒。一个信使嘟囔着把你的名字写上了板。|你飞观星台航线，在钟楼边抄了近道，以一口气的优势打破了新纪录。阁楼一片欢呼；原纪录保持者生起了闷气。|你如今熟悉所有近道。你的名字以很大的粉笔字写在了图书馆航线一栏。}
# en: {You take the corner by the bell tower too fast and meet a gutter. The parcel arrives; you arrive limping.|You're on pace until a gust shoves you into a flagpole. Your time goes on the board anyway, under the heading SLOWEST.|You misjudge the landing platform and skid the length of it on your knees. The couriers award you a record for distance.}
opt.left.say.2 [a7e12c] = {你在钟楼边转弯太快，撞上了一道排水槽。包裹到了；你一瘸一拐地到了。|你一直跟得上节奏，直到一阵风把你推向一根旗杆。你的时间照样上了板，列在“最慢”一栏。|你看错了起降台，跪着在上面滑了整整一个台长。信使们授予你一项距离纪录。}
# en: Study the routes instead
opt.right.label [acd663] = 改为研究航线
# en: {You copy down every route on the board and the wind notes beside them. You won't break a record today, but you'll know how.|You ask the couriers how each record was flown. Three of the stories are lies; you can tell which.|You sit under the board working out a new route to the village. It might be a minute faster. Might.}
opt.right.say.1 [c31313] = {你把板上每条航线和旁边的风向注记都抄了下来。今天你破不了纪录，但你会知道怎么破。|你问信使们每项纪录是怎么飞出来的。其中三个故事是假的；你分辨得出是哪三个。|你坐在板下琢磨一条去镇上的新航线。也许能快一分钟。也许。}

@event courier_loft_pigeon_strike
# en: The Pigeons Are on Strike
title [4c9e50] = 鸽子罢工了
# en: {The loft's message pigeons are on strike. They sit on the rafter in a row, puffed and silent, beside a list of demands scratched in claw-marks.|The pigeons have struck again. The demands have grown: better grain, a window that shuts, and the removal of a particular courier.|The pigeons are on strike. They look at you as you come in, as if you've been appointed to negotiate.} {The undelivered notes are piling up.|One pigeon is plainly the ringleader; it has a bald patch and a stare.|{season == "winter": The window that doesn't shut is letting the snow in, which seems fair.|Every courier in the loft is pretending not to be afraid of the ringleader.}}
text [a71cd2] = {阁楼的信鸽罢工了。它们在椽子上排成一排，鼓着毛一声不吭，旁边是一张用爪印刻出的诉求清单。|鸽子又罢工了。诉求变多了：更好的谷子、一扇关得上的窗，以及开除某位信使。|鸽子在罢工。你一进门它们就看着你，好像你被任命去谈判。} {没送出去的字条越堆越高。|有一只显然是头目：秃了一块，眼神很凶。|{season == "winter": 那扇关不上的窗正往里飘雪，这似乎很公平。|阁楼里每个信使都装作不怕那个头目。}}
# en: A row of indignant pigeons sitting in a line on a loft rafter beside a scrap of paper listing their demands in tiny claw-marks.
scene [55ffc3] = 一排愤愤不平的鸽子蹲在阁楼椽子上，旁边一张纸片上用细小的爪印列着它们的诉求。
# en: Talk the ringleader round
opt.left.label [4ac3df] = 劝服鸽子头目
# en: {You offer seed, flattery and a promise about the window. The ringleader considers, coos once, and the strike is over.|You talk to the ringleader as you'd talk to a magistrate. It accepts your terms and a raisin.|The ringleader hears you out, eye to eye. The pigeons rise in a clatter and the backlog flies.}
opt.left.say.1 [f74c40] = {你献上谷子、恭维和一个关于窗户的承诺。头目考虑片刻，咕了一声，罢工结束了。|你像跟一位地方法官说话一样跟头目谈。它接受了你的条件和一颗葡萄干。|头目和你四目相对，听你说完。鸽子们扑棱棱飞起，积压的信件全飞走了。}
# en: {The ringleader hears your offer and pecks your knuckle, hard. Talks have broken down.|The whole rafter turns its back on you, in unison, which is very hard to recover from. One of them nips your ear on the way.|They accept the raisin and refuse the terms. One of them sits on your head, claws first, to make the point.}
opt.left.say.2 [37fa4b] = {头目听完你的提议，狠狠啄了你的指关节一口。谈判破裂。|整排椽子齐刷刷背过身去，这很难挽回。其中一只顺路啄了你的耳朵。|它们收下了葡萄干，拒绝了条件。有一只爪子朝下坐到你头上，以示立场。}
# en: Carry their notes by hand
opt.right.label [f70187] = 亲手送它们的信
# en: {You run the undelivered notes round the castle yourself, all seven towers, and come back with sore legs and the pigeons' quiet contempt.|You deliver the notes on foot. The pigeons watch you go, smug as landladies. Your feet ache by the last tower.|You run the round on foot again. You're faster than a pigeon on the stairs, if not in the air, and your calves know it.}
opt.right.say.1 [eb1897] = {你亲自把没送出的字条送遍城堡七座塔，回来时腿酸了，还收获了鸽子们无声的鄙视。|你步行送信。鸽子们看着你走，得意得像女房东。到最后一座塔时你的脚生疼。|你又步行送了一圈。上楼梯你比鸽子快，在天上可不行，你的小腿肚很清楚。}
